{"id":"w39454","name":"Chinese Chews (Nut and Date Bars)","author":"Wikibooks Cookbook contributors","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Chinese_Chews_(Nut_and_Date_Bars)"},"via":{"name":"Wikibooks","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Chinese_Chews_(Nut_and_Date_Bars)"},"image":"","cuisine":"Caribbean","country":"","region":"Americas","course":"dessert","protein":"veggie","diet":2,"allergens":21,"minutes":45,"time":{"prep":15,"cook":30,"passive":0,"passiveWhy":[]},"timeEstimated":false,"servings":"4","difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"item":"2 eggs","qty":""},{"item":"⅔ cup sugar","qty":""},{"item":"⅔ cup self-raising flour","qty":""},{"item":"⅓ tsp salt","qty":""},{"item":"1 tsp vanilla","qty":""},{"item":"½ cup chopped dates","qty":""},{"item":"½ cup seedless raisins","qty":""},{"item":"¾ cup chopped walnuts","qty":""},{"item":"Icing sugar to taste","qty":""}],"steps":["Beat eggs until foamy. Add sugar and mix.","Add flour and salt.","Add vanilla, then the fruit and nuts. Mix well.","Spread in greased 8-inch cake pan.","Bake for about 30–35 minutes at 350°F (175°C) until golden brown.","Cut into squares while still warm. Roll in icing sugar."],"tags":[],"youtube":"","culture":{"text":"Chinese chews are a bar cookie containing nuts and dried fruit. They have a chewy consistency.","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Chinese_Chews_(Nut_and_Date_Bars)"}},"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}